# Component styling files

Every component folder has a `styles.ts`. The component file owns structure and behavior;
`styles.ts` owns every Tailwind class, `cva()` variant, and shadcn `className`.

## What lives in `styles.ts`

- Every Tailwind class string, including one-liners (`flex`, `gap-2`, a single color).
- `cva()` variant tables and their exported `VariantProps` type.
- `cn()`-composed class strings and class-building helpers.
- Style-only constants: variant maps and size/intent enums used only for class selection.

```ts
// button/styles.ts
import { cva, type VariantProps } from 'class-variance-authority';

export const buttonVariants = cva(
  'inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md text-sm font-medium transition-colors',
  {
    variants: {
      intent: {
        primary: 'bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90',
        danger: 'bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground hover:bg-destructive/90',
      },
      size: { sm: 'h-8 px-3', md: 'h-10 px-4' },
    },
    defaultVariants: { intent: 'primary', size: 'md' },
  },
);

export type ButtonVariants = VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants>;
```

```tsx
// button/button.tsx
import { cn } from '@/shared/lib/utils';
import { buttonVariants, type ButtonVariants } from './styles';

type ButtonProps = React.ComponentProps<'button'> & ButtonVariants;

export const Button = ({ intent, size, className, ...props }: ButtonProps): JSX.Element => {
  return <button className={cn(buttonVariants({ intent, size }), className)} {...props} />;
};
```

## What stays out of `styles.ts`

- Business logic, event handlers, hooks, and data fetching.
- Structural JSX. Styling decides how a node looks, not what the tree contains.
- Tailwind class strings in component JSX. There is no inline-class exception.

## Contract

- `styles.ts` exports plain values and, when variants exist, the derived `VariantProps` type.
- The component passes an incoming `className` into that export so a caller can still override.
- Colors are semantic tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`). No raw hex or palette-step classes.
- One light palette. No `dark:` variants.

Load `tailwind-styles` for `cva()` authoring and `shadcn-usage` for primitive composition.
